    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, welcome. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S009",
      "patient_response": "Well, I'm here because I just keep forgetting things I really shouldn’t be forgetting. Important stuff, you know? Like my heart follow-up appointments, or remembering to call the clinic back when they leave a message. Or I'll go to do a repair job around the house and show up without the right tools. \n\nWhich reminds me, I was looking for my good socket wrench the other day, the old Craftsman one. They don't make 'em like that anymore, you know? Everything you buy now is cheap metal that strips the second you put some actual elbow grease into it. I got that wrench at Sears back in maybe '85. Man, I miss Sears. Used to be you could buy a washing machine, a pair of work boots, and a lawnmower all in one trip. My wife and I would go down there just about every Saturday to walk around the mall... \n\nWait, what did you ask me? Oh, right, why I'm here. Yeah, just... forgetting the important things, mostly.",
