    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Did you notice these memory problems start suddenly, or have they developed slowly over time?",
      "targeted_symptom": "duration",
      "patient_response": "Well, it wasn't really a slow thing, but it wasn't overnight either. I'd say it's been causing me real trouble for about a year and two months. That was right around the time I had my cardiac scare. Scared the absolute daylights out of my wife, let me tell you. After that, the doctors made me cut way back on my walking and my garage projects—which is really the stuff that always used to keep me settled, you know? \n\nI used to walk all over this neighborhood. Three miles a day, easy. Down past the old elementary school, right through the park... they put in those new benches at the park, by the way. Just terrible design. They're made of that recycled plastic material that gets hotter than a frying pan in the summer. I sat on one back in July and practically burned my jeans off. I mean, who approves these things? The city council just throws money at whatever sounds good on paper, but they don't think about the practical application of it at all. My buddy Tom went to a town hall meeting to complain about it, but they wouldn't even give him the microphone. \n\nAnyway... what was I saying? Oh, right, the timeline. Yeah, about a year and two months, ever since the heart thing made me stop moving around so much.",
